#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# find_transient_repeat

#% text
# `find_transient_repeat(xs, k)` gives `[transient, block]`: the shortest initial part after which xs repeats the shortest block at least k times, a partial last copy allowed.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# When no block repeats k times the value is `[xs, []]`. Strings give strings.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
find_transient_repeat([1, 2, 3, 4, 3, 4, 3, 4], 3)
#% output
#= [[1, 2], [3, 4]]

#% cell
find_transient_repeat([1, 2, 3, 4, 3, 4, 3, 4], 4)
#% output
#= [[1, 2, 3, 4, 3, 4, 3, 4], []]

#% cell
find_transient_repeat("abcdedede", 2)
#% output
#= ["abc", "de"]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `find_repeat`
